#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "SPANK plugin user guide {#spank-plugin-user-guide}"
msgstr "Panduan pengguna plugin SPANK {#spank-plugin-user-guide}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The [SPANK plugin](https://github.com/qiskit-community/spank-plugins/) for the [Quantum Resource Management Interface (QRMI)](/guides/qrmi) is used to configure access to quantum resources from user jobs in a compute environment administrated by the [Slurm](https://slurm.schedmd.com/quickstart.html) workload manager. This is a guide for plugin users to configure QPU resource allocation when creating Slurm jobs.\n"
msgstr "[Plugin SPANK](https://github.com/qiskit-community/spank-plugins/) untuk [Quantum Resource Management Interface (QRMI)](/guides/qrmi) digunakan untuk mengkonfigurasi akses kepada sumber kuantum daripada kerja pengguna dalam persekitaran pengkomputeran yang ditadbir oleh pengurus beban kerja [Slurm](https://slurm.schedmd.com/quickstart.html). Ini ialah panduan untuk pengguna plugin mengkonfigurasi peruntukan sumber QPU semasa mencipta kerja Slurm.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Slurm QPU resource definitions determine what physical resources can be used by Slurm jobs in high-performance compute (HPC) environments. User source code should be agnostic to specific backend instances, and even backend types whenever possible. This keeps source code portable while the QPU selection criteria are part of the resource definition (which is considered configuration rather than source code).\n"
msgstr "Definisi sumber QPU Slurm menentukan sumber fizikal yang boleh digunakan oleh kerja Slurm dalam persekitaran pengkomputeran berprestasi tinggi (HPC). Kod sumber pengguna sepatutnya tidak bergantung pada contoh Backend tertentu, malah jenis Backend jika boleh. Ini memastikan kod sumber mudah alih sementara kriteria pemilihan QPU adalah sebahagian daripada definisi sumber (yang dianggap sebagai konfigurasi dan bukan kod sumber).\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Configure QPU resources in job creation {#configure-qpu-resources-in-job-creation}"
msgstr "Konfigurasi sumber QPU dalam penciptaan kerja {#configure-qpu-resources-in-job-creation}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"caution\">\n"
"Note that this plugin is under active development and the exact syntax is subject to change.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"caution\">\n"
"Perhatikan bahawa plugin ini sedang dalam pembangunan aktif dan sintaks tepat boleh berubah.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Administrator scope {#administrator-scope}"
msgstr "Skop pentadbir {#administrator-scope}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"HPC administrators configure the SPANK plugin to specify what physical resources can be provided to Slurm jobs.\n"
"This configuration contains all the information needed to have Slurm jobs access the physical resources, such as endpoints and access credentials.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pentadbir HPC mengkonfigurasi plugin SPANK untuk menentukan sumber fizikal yang boleh diberikan kepada kerja Slurm.\n"
"Konfigurasi ini mengandungi semua maklumat yang diperlukan supaya kerja Slurm boleh mengakses sumber fizikal, seperti titik akhir dan kelayakan akses.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Read the [`qrmi_config.json.example`](https://github.com/qiskit-community/spank-plugins/blob/main/plugins/spank_qrmi/qrmi_config.json.example) for a comprehensive example configuration.\n"
msgstr "Baca [`qrmi_config.json.example`](https://github.com/qiskit-community/spank-plugins/blob/main/plugins/spank_qrmi/qrmi_config.json.example) untuk contoh konfigurasi yang komprehensif.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In `slurm.conf`, QPU resources can be assigned to some or all nodes for usage:\n"
msgstr "Dalam `slurm.conf`, sumber QPU boleh diberikan kepada sebahagian atau semua nod untuk digunakan:\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "User scope {#user-scope}"
msgstr "Skop pengguna {#user-scope}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "HPC users submit jobs using QPU resources that are tied to Slurm QPU resources. The name attribute references what the HPC administrator has defined. During a Slurm job's runtime, backend selection can be based on criteria other than a predefined name referring to a specific backend (for example, by capacity and error rate qualifiers, to help down-select among the defined set of backends).\n"
msgstr "Pengguna HPC menghantar kerja menggunakan sumber QPU yang dikaitkan dengan sumber QPU Slurm. Atribut nama merujuk kepada apa yang telah ditakrifkan oleh pentadbir HPC. Semasa masa jalan kerja Slurm, pemilihan Backend boleh berdasarkan kriteria selain nama yang telah ditetapkan yang merujuk kepada Backend tertentu (contohnya, menggunakan kelayakan kapasiti dan kadar ralat, untuk membantu memilih daripada set Backend yang ditakrifkan).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "There might be additional environment variables required, depending on the backend type.\n"
msgstr "Mungkin ada pemboleh ubah persekitaran tambahan yang diperlukan, bergantung pada jenis Backend.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`SBATCH` parameters will point to one or more QPU resources assigned to the application as generic resources.\n"
"Environment variables provided through the plugin will provide the necessary information to the application (see the [HPC application scope](#hpc-application-scope) section for details).\n"
msgstr ""
"Parameter `SBATCH` akan menunjuk kepada satu atau lebih sumber QPU yang diberikan kepada aplikasi sebagai sumber generik.\n"
"Pemboleh ubah persekitaran yang disediakan melalui plugin akan menyediakan maklumat yang diperlukan kepada aplikasi (lihat bahagian [Skop aplikasi HPC](#hpc-application-scope) untuk butiran).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To use more QPU resources, add more QPUs to the `--qpu` parameter:\n"
msgstr "Untuk menggunakan lebih banyak sumber QPU, tambahkan lebih banyak QPU pada parameter `--qpu`:\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "HPC application scope {#hpc-application-scope}"
msgstr "Skop aplikasi HPC {#hpc-application-scope}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "HPC applications use the Slurm QPU resources assigned to the Slurm job.\n"
msgstr "Aplikasi HPC menggunakan sumber QPU Slurm yang diberikan kepada kerja Slurm.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Environment variables provide more details for use by the application; for example, `SLURM_JOB_QPU_RESOURCES` lists the quantum resource names (comma-separated if several are provided).\n"
"These variables will be used by QRMI. (See the README files in the various QRMI directories ([IBM](https://github.com/qiskit-community/qrmi/blob/main/examples/qiskit_primitives/ibm/README.md), [pasqal](https://github.com/qiskit-community/qrmi/blob/main/examples/qiskit_primitives/pasqal/README.md)) for more details.)\n"
msgstr ""
"Pemboleh ubah persekitaran memberikan butiran lanjut untuk digunakan oleh aplikasi; contohnya, `SLURM_JOB_QPU_RESOURCES` menyenaraikan nama sumber kuantum (dipisahkan koma jika beberapa diberikan).\n"
"Pemboleh ubah ini akan digunakan oleh QRMI. (Lihat fail README dalam pelbagai direktori QRMI ([IBM](https://github.com/qiskit-community/qrmi/blob/main/examples/qiskit_primitives/ibm/README.md), [pasqal](https://github.com/qiskit-community/qrmi/blob/main/examples/qiskit_primitives/pasqal/README.md)) untuk butiran lanjut.)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "See the [examples directory](https://github.com/qiskit-community/qrmi/tree/main/examples/qiskit_primitives/) for example files.\n"
msgstr "Lihat [direktori contoh](https://github.com/qiskit-community/qrmi/tree/main/examples/qiskit_primitives/) untuk fail contoh.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Backend specifics {#backend-specifics}"
msgstr "Spesifik Backend {#backend-specifics}"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "IBM Quantum System API {#ibm-quantum-system-api}"
msgstr "IBM Quantum System API {#ibm-quantum-system-api}"

#. type: Title #####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Administrator scope {#administrator-scope-1}"
msgstr "Skop pentadbir {#administrator-scope-1}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Configuration of Quantum System API backends (HPC admin scope) includes endpoints and credentials to the Quantum System endpoint and authentication services, as well as to the S3 endpoint.\n"
"Specifically, this includes:\n"
msgstr ""
"Konfigurasi Backend API Sistem Kuantum (skop pentadbir HPC) termasuk titik akhir dan kelayakan kepada titik akhir Quantum System dan perkhidmatan pengesahan, serta titik akhir S3.\n"
"Secara khusus, ini termasuk:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "IBM Cloud&reg; API key for creating bearer tokens\n"
msgstr "Kunci API IBM Cloud&reg; untuk mencipta token pembawa\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Endpoint of the Quantum System API\n"
msgstr "Titik akhir API Sistem Kuantum\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "S3 bucket and access details\n"
msgstr "Baldi S3 dan butiran akses\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Access credentials should not be visible to HPC users or other non-privileged users on the system.\n"
"Therefore, sensitive data can be put in separate files, which can be access-protected accordingly.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kelayakan akses tidak sepatutnya kelihatan kepada pengguna HPC atau pengguna bukan istimewa lain pada sistem.\n"
"Oleh itu, data sensitif boleh diletakkan dalam fail berasingan, yang boleh dilindungi dengan sewajarnya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Note that Slurm has full access to the backend.\n"
"This has several implications:\n"
msgstr ""
"Perhatikan bahawa Slurm mempunyai akses penuh kepada Backend.\n"
"Ini mempunyai beberapa implikasi:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Slurm plugin is responsible for multi-tenancy (ensuring that users don't see results of other users' jobs)\n"
msgstr "Plugin Slurm bertanggungjawab untuk multi-tenancy (memastikan pengguna tidak melihat keputusan kerja pengguna lain)\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The HPC cluster side is responsible for vetting users (who is allowed to access the QPU) and ensuring according access\n"
msgstr "Pihak kluster HPC bertanggungjawab untuk menyaring pengguna (siapa yang dibenarkan mengakses QPU) dan memastikan akses yang sesuai\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The capacity and priority of the QPU usage is solely managed through Slurm; there is no other scheduling of users involved outside of Slurm\n"
msgstr "Kapasiti dan keutamaan penggunaan QPU diurus sepenuhnya melalui Slurm; tiada penjadualan pengguna lain di luar Slurm\n"

#. type: Title #####
#, no-wrap
msgid "User scope {#user-scope-1}"
msgstr "Skop pengguna {#user-scope-1}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Execution lanes are not exposed to the HPC administrator or user directly.\n"
"Instead, during runtime, there can be two different modes that HPC users can specify:\n"
msgstr ""
"Lorong pelaksanaan tidak dedahkan kepada pentadbir atau pengguna HPC secara langsung.\n"
"Sebaliknya, semasa masa jalan, terdapat dua mod berbeza yang boleh ditentukan oleh pengguna HPC:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`exclusive=true` specifies that no other jobs can use the resource at the same time. An exclusive mode job gets all execution lanes and cannot run at the same time as a non-exclusive job\n"
msgstr "`exclusive=true` menentukan bahawa tiada kerja lain boleh menggunakan sumber pada masa yang sama. Kerja mod eksklusif mendapat semua lorong pelaksanaan dan tidak boleh berjalan pada masa yang sama dengan kerja bukan eksklusif\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`exclusive=false` allows other jobs to run in parallel. In this case, there can be as many jobs as there are execution lanes, all running at the same time, and the job is assigned one lane\n"
msgstr "`exclusive=false` membenarkan kerja lain berjalan secara selari. Dalam kes ini, boleh ada seberapa banyak kerja sebanyak terdapat lorong pelaksanaan, semua berjalan pada masa yang sama, dan kerja diberikan satu lorong\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "IBM Quantum Compute Service {#ibm-quantum-compute-service}"
msgstr "IBM Quantum Compute Service {#ibm-quantum-compute-service}"

#. type: Title #####
#, no-wrap
msgid "User scope {#user-scope-2}"
msgstr "Skop pengguna {#user-scope-2}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It is expected that users specify additional access details in environment variables.\n"
"Specifically, this includes the following:\n"
msgstr ""
"Dijangkakan bahawa pengguna menentukan butiran akses tambahan dalam pemboleh ubah persekitaran.\n"
"Secara khusus, ini termasuk yang berikut:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "IBM Quantum Compute Service instance (CRN, Cloud Resource Name)\n"
msgstr "Contoh IBM Quantum Compute Service (CRN, Cloud Resource Name)\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Endpoint for Quantum Compute (unless auto-detected from the CRN)\n"
msgstr "Titik akhir untuk Quantum Compute (kecuali dikesan secara automatik daripada CRN)\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "API key, which has access to the CRN\n"
msgstr "Kunci API, yang mempunyai akses kepada CRN\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "S3 instance, bucket, and access token/credentials for data transfers\n"
msgstr "Contoh S3, baldi, dan token akses/kelayakan untuk pemindahan data\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"These details determine under which user and service instance IBM Quantum Compute Service is used.\n"
"Accordingly, IBM Quantum&reg; Platform scheduling considers the user's and service instance's capabilities for scheduling.\n"
msgstr ""
"Butiran ini menentukan di bawah pengguna dan contoh perkhidmatan mana IBM Quantum Compute Service digunakan.\n"
"Dengan demikian, penjadualan IBM Quantum® Platform mempertimbangkan keupayaan pengguna dan contoh perkhidmatan untuk penjadualan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "At this time, users must provide the above details (no shared cluster-wide quantum access).\n"
msgstr "Pada masa ini, pengguna mesti menyediakan butiran di atas (tiada akses kuantum bersama seluruh kluster).\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pasqal Cloud Services {#pasqal-cloud-services}"
msgstr "Perkhidmatan Awan Pasqal {#pasqal-cloud-services}"

#. type: Title #####
#, no-wrap
msgid "HPC admin scope {#hpc-admin-scope}"
msgstr "Skop pentadbir HPC {#hpc-admin-scope}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "There is no specific setup required from HPC admins for PCS usage.\n"
msgstr "Tiada persediaan khusus yang diperlukan daripada pentadbir HPC untuk penggunaan PCS.\n"

#. type: Title #####
#, no-wrap
msgid "HPC user scope {#hpc-user-scope}"
msgstr "Skop pengguna HPC {#hpc-user-scope}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It is expected that users specify additional access details in environment variables.\n"
"Currently, this includes the following:\n"
msgstr ""
"Dijangkakan bahawa pengguna menentukan butiran akses tambahan dalam pemboleh ubah persekitaran.\n"
"Pada masa ini, ini termasuk yang berikut:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "PCS resource to target (FRESNEL, EMU_FRESNEL, EMU_MPS)\n"
msgstr "Sumber PCS untuk disasarkan (FRESNEL, EMU_FRESNEL, EMU_MPS)\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Authorization token\n"
msgstr "Token kebenaran\n"
